12. SAFETY, RF AND EXPERIMENTAL-HARDWARE WARNING

The Project Materials are experimental electronics.  Parts of the
counter firmware operate an STM32F103 above its 72 MHz specified
system-clock limit, and the VHF/UHF transmitter circuit can generate
radio-frequency energy.  Results can vary by silicon, board, waveform,
layout, components, temperature and test equipment.  Experimental
"MHz EXP" readings are not certification of an emitted fundamental.

You are solely responsible for safe construction and operation, input
voltage limits, anti-static handling, thermal and electrical safety,
spectrum authorisation, interference prevention and compliance with
every law and regulation that applies where you build or operate the
hardware.  Do not connect an antenna or transmit unless you are
legally authorised and the equipment, frequency, power, emissions and
operating conditions are lawful.  Prefer a properly rated dummy load,
shielded test setup and suitable measurement equipment.

